# edi-run DECISIONS.log — newest at TOP

## 2026-11-18 — Review bar demoted from standing gate to tiered (Owner: S2)

**Ruling.** The hardening sprint is over; the last three changes were flip-a-default
scale, and carrying a deep + adversarial frontier review pair as a standing gate on
every change was drifting toward the Plumbline failure mode (ceremony growing faster
than evidence). Tiered bar, effective now:

- **Deep + adversarial frontier reviews** — required only for changes touching
  `adapters.py` or gate semantics (gates.py, loop.py freeze/finalize paths).
- **Everything else** — full suite + probe gate + CI green. Those already catch the
  invariant regressions; reviews add no marginal signal at this change size.
- Review-artifact tests are re-homed by CONCERN (tests/test_sandbox.py,
  tests/test_briefing.py), never stacked as dated strata per review round.

## 2026-11-18 — S1 sandbox.reads default flipped to allowlist (Owner: S2, decision A)

**Ruling.** bwrap jobs default to `sandbox.reads=allowlist`. Denylist remains available
by explicit config and remains the seatbelt (macOS) posture, whose allowlist mode is
not shippable on this OS build (deny-precedence is order-decided and deny-default with
allow-exceptions aborts sandbox-exec — verified by execution, PR #16).

**Evidence at ruling time.** Local suite 66 tests OK (1 skip: macOS leg). Probe gate
14 PASS / 0 FAIL / 1 KNOWN-FAIL (S1 macOS-only known-fail) / 5 SKIP (S3, S4, S7–S9 are
bwrap/Linux). CI legs (Ubuntu bwrap) green: run 44294653521 against commit 131f888.

**Commit.** 131f888 `Owner ruling 2026-11-18 (A): bwrap sandbox.reads defaults to allowlist`

**Open.** macOS seatbelt allowlist via scoped-deny enumeration — named unexplored; if
shipped, it lands as a separate ruling. S7–S9 probes still gate CI green on Linux legs.
